      "url": "https://eos.org/articles/antarcticas-only-flowering-plants-take-opposite-paths-under-experimental-warming",
      "title": "Antarctic grass and pearlwort show opposite responses to experimental warming",
      "content_html": "A seven-year field experiment on King George Island found that Antarctica’s only two native flowering plants responded in opposite ways to warming: Antarctic hair grass showed reduced water flow through its leaves and lower photosynthesis, while Antarctic pearlwort showed increases in both. The findings come from plants grown in open-top chambers near Poland’s Henryk Arctowski Antarctic Station.\n\nThe chambers produced sharp temperature swings, not just higher average temperatures: during the 2018–19 summer, plants inside spent far more time below freezing than those outside. Researchers are now examining plants that have remained in the chambers for 16 years, along with microorganisms living around them.",
