      "id": "https://hu.euronews.com/2026/10/26/sved-kormany-letiltja-a-chatgpt-t-es-a-claude-ot-ez-az-oka",
      "url": "https://hu.euronews.com/2026/10/26/sved-kormany-letiltja-a-chatgpt-t-es-a-claude-ot-ez-az-oka",
      "title": "Sweden blocks ChatGPT and Claude on government computers over data risks",
      "content_html": "Sweden’s Government Offices blocked browser access to OpenAI’s ChatGPT and Anthropic’s Claude on employees’ work computers on Oct. 26. Microsoft Copilot remains approved, and some staff can still use the two restricted services through a dedicated government AI-assistant platform. The restriction applies to the central government offices, not to the public or every Swedish government body.\n\nOfficials cited information-security concerns about using AI services without agreements governing data protection and processing. A review of AI use at the Swedish Transport Administration earlier in 2026 found problems with the information staff entered and how they handled AI-generated responses. Officials warned that sensitive information might be stored or used for training, but the reports describe a risk, not a confirmed data leak.\n\nThe Government Offices says staff can continue using AI under tighter controls. Similar restrictions are in place at Sweden’s Tax Agency and National Board of Institutional Care, while the Swedish Enforcement Authority is reviewing the issue.",
