      "title": "RAMSA Unveils Plans for New Welcome Hall at Chicago’s Griffin Museum of Science and Industry",
      "content_html": "<p>RAMSA (<a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/office/robert-am-stern-architects\">Robert A.M. Stern Architects</a>) has unveiled the design for a new Welcome Hall at the Kenneth C. Griffin Museum of Science and Industry (Griffin MSI) in <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/chicago\">Chicago</a>, <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/illinois/page/1\">Illinois</a>. The project involves reopening the building's historic North Portico as a year-round entrance and introducing a new glazed volume connecting the portico to the <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/museum/page/1\">museum</a>'s exhibition spaces. The proposal is part of a master plan completed by RAMSA in 2024 that examines the use of the museum's existing exhibition and public areas.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-27T06:30:00+00:00",
